    "created_at": "2016-12-06T00:45:14Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-12-06T00:45:14Z",
    "body": "In general I managed to confuse myself a bit about what level should be handling the censoring of unpaired surrogates. The tests show that censoring happens, but maybe in browsers it's in the text/plain serialization algorithm, or the other possible serialization algorithms? Maybe it's there already, but I'm having trouble understanding the spec switching between WTF-16 strings/abstract strings/byte sequences?\r\n\r\nThe worst that can happen is that this change is redundant though, so probably we should still merge it.",
